\section{The status codes}{


\code{STATUS_PRIMARY} (\code{"P"}), \code{STATUS_CREDENTIALED} (\code{"C"}), \code{STATUS_TELEMED}
(\code{"T"}) and \code{STATUS_INACTIVE} (a single space) are the four values a
crosstab cell can hold. Blank is a \emph{meaningful} status, not a missing value
-- see \code{STATUS_LABELS} -- which is why the crosstab fills gaps with it
rather than leaving them \code{NA}.
}

\section{Two telemedicine constants, deliberately}{


\code{TELEMED_SUBSTRING} (\code{"TELEMED"}) is what the classifier looks for \emph{inside}
a status category when deciding a facility's status. \code{TELEMED_CATEGORY}
(\code{"TELEMEDICINE AFFILIATE"}) is the exact, full category name that defines
the report population. The second is stricter than the first on purpose.
}

\section{Program text cleanup}{


\code{PROGRAM_TEXT_DROP_PATTERN} and \code{PROGRAM_TEXT_COLLAPSE_PATTERN} are the SAS
\code{compbl(compress(x, , 'kads'))} pair: \code{kads} keeps alphabetic, digit and
space characters and drops everything else; \code{compbl} then collapses runs of
blanks to one.
}

